{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqi8j0n8lak","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"re dispatched task reuses stale worktree and forks old base","summary":"When re-dispatching an orchestrator task that had a PRIOR attempt, telling the worker to \"reuse the existing worktree if present\" makes it fork from that STALE worktree's base commit, not the current feature/main head. Observed live: S8 (/22) reused its pre-/25 worktree (merge-base 46d0b71) so its arms.py never had /25's eager-judge rewrite and diverged → merge_attempt conflicted on arms.py. PREVENTION (dispatcher duty): before re-dispatching a task with a prior attempt, either remove_worktree the stale attempt so branch_task re-forks from the CURRENT base head, or have the worker VERIFY the fork point (grep a known marker that only exists at the intended head) and STOP if absent. Base/worktree freshness is the dispatcher's responsibility, same as wiring.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-17T15:37:46.244Z","vec":[-0.061189569532871246,0.002190707018598914,0.08571580052375793,0.018239282071590424,0.005230440758168697,-0.07637538015842438,-0.04343197122216225,-0.027671804651618004,0.0005219639278948307,0.024904349818825722,-0.0007201095577329397,0.04239918664097786,-0.05722196027636528,-0.0012476193951442838,-0.030813466757535934,-0.03483543172478676,0.029451875016093254,-0.026537258177995682,0.033162541687488556,-0.05259731411933899,0.016551842913031578,0.04282603785395622,-0.005172494798898697,0.03167064115405083,0.03712943196296692,-0.07618419826030731,-0.08472438156604767,0.0007065013633109629,0.009459967724978924,-0.024545863270759583,0.019429411739110947,0.09646732360124588,-0.07513995468616486,-0.05003364011645317,0.034714724868535995,0.15119019150733948,0.020788803696632385,-0.044648729264736176,0.0066245486959815025,0.01773074083030224,0.034913551062345505,0.06441209465265274,-0.03324379399418831,-0.014318718574941158,-0.0785633996129036,0.016255447641015053,-0.010481178760528564,-0.0359791740775108